; E170 W0.2 -- the floor's first observable root WITH AN IMPORT.
;
; Every other file in this directory that the test floor observes is import-free,
; and that was not a style choice: `observe` compiled ONE FILE with no resolution
; step, so the six import-free samples were the only ones it could reach and they
; are exactly test-runner.chiral's manifest. 62 of the 68 files here import
; something, and a chirality-in-chirality test needs `prelude` at minimum, so the floor
; could not observe a single one of the programs E170 migrates.
;
; This root is the positive control for the fix. It USES what it imports --
; `max`/`min` are prelude defs, not prims -- so it cannot compile from its own
; bytes alone: hand this file to `compile-all` unresolved and the answer is
; `load: unknown name max`, i.e. `ob-nobuild`. Observing it as `ob-exit 42` is
; therefore a claim that resolution actually ran.
(import "prelude/prelude")

(def main (-> I64 I64)
  (lam (n) (max 42 (min 7 3))))
